GetCurrentExit [SimTalk]
Returns the number of the side at which the MU exits the Converter designated by <Path>.
Remarks
The figures below illustrate the sides depending on the direction in which you inserted the Converter into
your simulation model. The numbers designate the side of the Converter at which the MU exits.
Type
Read-only attribute
Syntax
<Path>.GetCurrentExit → integer
Return Value
The return value has the data type integer.
Example
No := ?.GetCurrentExit
GetCurrentExit [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 11-2289
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

