IsUp [SimTalk] - Converter
Returns if the Converter designated by <Path> is in the up position (true) or in the down position (false).
Type
Read-only attribute
Syntax
<Path>.IsUp → boolean
Return Value
The return value has the data type boolean.
Example
PosUpDown := MyConverter.IsUp
You can also use the attribute IsUp to start the lifting process.
Example
MyConverter.IsUp := true
IsUp [SimTalk] - Converter
Plant Simulation Help 11-2291
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

StatMovingEmptyPortion [SimTalk]
Returns the portion of the statistics collection period during which the Converter designated by <Path>
was raising or lowering itself and was not conveying a MU.
Type
Read-only attribute
Syntax
<Path>.StatMovingEmptyPortion → real
Return Value
The return value has the data type real.
Example
print Converter.StatMovingEmptyPortion
